{
  "_readme": [
    "Blueprint for the guest demo data. This file is the only hand-written input to the pipeline;",
    "everything downstream is either model output or the learner translations authored in",
    "scripts/.demo-out/answers.json.",
    "",
    "Pipeline:  generate-demo-sources.mjs -> author-demo-answers.mjs -> (author by hand)",
    "           -> grade-demo-sessions.mjs -> freeze-demo-sessions.mjs -> data/demo/*.json",
    "",
    "Source texts always come from the app's own /api/generate so that nothing third-party",
    "ships in a public repository.",
    "",
    "The sidebar filters sessions by the currently selected study language (components/layout/",
    "Sidebar.tsx:49), and the app defaults to es -> en. That is why es carries six sessions",
    "covering all four practice modes, while the other languages carry one each: they exist to",
    "prove multi-language support when the viewer switches the language selector.",
    "",
    "'grading.attempted' is a count or \"all\"; segments past it stay neutral and produce a",
    "partial progress ring. 'yellow'/'red' are TARGETS, not facts — the real grader decides,",
    "and grading-review.md reports every disagreement.",
    "",
    "Most sessions are deliberately left part-finished. /api/translate splits these texts into",
    "~20 segments, and twenty-out-of-twenty graded on every card would read as a demo account",
    "rather than a practice log — a real learner has more sessions on the go than finished. The",
    "pinned skit is the one that is complete, so the sidebar still shows a full green ring."
  ],
